# QuickNotes 📝

## Project Description
QuickNotes is a simple, responsive note-taking web application built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It allows users to create, organize, search, and delete notes easily.

## Features
- Add notes with a category: Personal, Work, or Study.
- Validate notes to ensure they contain between 1 and 200 characters.
- Delete individual notes.
- Search notes by text, regardless of uppercase or lowercase letters.
- Display the total number of notes.
- Save notes in the browser using localStorage.
- Responsive design for desktop and mobile devices.

## Technologies Used
- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript
- Browser localStorage

## Project Structure
```text
quicknotes-app/
├── index.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
└── README.md
```

## How to Run the Project
1. Download or clone this repository.
2. Open `index.html` in your browser.
3. Add notes, choose categories, search, and delete notes.

Alternatively, use the Live Server extension in Visual Studio Code.

## Storage
QuickNotes uses the browser's localStorage to save notes. Notes remain available after refreshing the page in the same browser and on the same device.

